sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant TLS as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP TLS 1.2+
    participant AuthN as Authentication Filter<br/>WithAuthentication
    participant OIDC as OIDC Provider<br/>(if configured)
    participant K8sAuthN as Kubernetes API<br/>TokenReview<br/>authentication.k8s.io/v1
    participant AuthZ as Authorization Filter<br/>WithAuthorization
    participant K8sAuthZ as Kubernetes API<br/>SubjectAccessReview<br/>authorization.k8s.io/v1
    participant Upstream as Upstream Service<br/>localhost:8080 HTTP

    Note over Client,Upstream: Inference / Metrics Request Flow

    Client->>TLS: HTTPS Request<br/>Port 8443, TLS 1.2+
    TLS->>AuthN: Decrypt & forward<br/>HTTP/2 or HTTP/1.1

    alt OIDC Authentication
        AuthN->>OIDC: Validate OIDC Token
        OIDC-->>AuthN: Token Valid / Identity
    else Delegating TokenReview
        AuthN->>K8sAuthN: POST TokenReview<br/>Bearer Token
        K8sAuthN-->>AuthN: Authenticated User Info
    end

    AuthN->>AuthZ: Authenticated Request<br/>User Identity

    Note over AuthZ: Union Authorizer Chain

    alt 1. Hardcoded Metrics Authorizer
        AuthZ->>AuthZ: Check well-known<br/>OpenShift metrics users
    else 2. Static Authorizer
        AuthZ->>AuthZ: Match config file<br/>resourceAttributes rules
    else 3. SAR Authorizer
        AuthZ->>K8sAuthZ: POST SubjectAccessReview<br/>User, Resource, Verb
        K8sAuthZ-->>AuthZ: Allowed / Denied
    end

    AuthZ->>Upstream: Reverse Proxy Forward<br/>HTTP localhost (h2c optional)
    Upstream-->>AuthZ: Response
    AuthZ-->>TLS: Response
    TLS-->>Client: HTTPS Response

    Note over Client,Upstream: Health Check Flow (Bypasses Auth)

    Client->>TLS: GET /healthz<br/>Proxy Endpoints Port
    TLS-->>Client: 200 OK
